en Avco Corporation, \na Delaware corporation, and certain of its employees at the Lycoming \nDivision Plant, Stratford, Connecticut, represented by International \nUnion, United Automobile, Aerospace and Agricultural Implement \nWorkers of America, AFL—CIO, and Locals 376 and 1010 thereof; and\nWHEREAS, such dispute threatens to result in a strike affecting a \nsubstantial part of an industry or industries of the United States \nengaged in trade, commerce, transportation, transmission, or communi­\ncation among the several states or with foreign nations, or engaged in \nthe production of goods for commerce, which strike, if permitted to \noccur or continue, would, in my opinion, imperil the national safety;\nNOW, THEREFORE, by virtue of the authority vested in me by \nSection.206 of the Labor Management Relations Act of 1947 (61 Stat. \n155 ; 29 U.S.C. 176), I  hereby create a board of inquiry, consisting of \nMr. Leo C. Brown, Chairman, Mr. James C. Hill and Mr. Clyde W. \nSummers, whom I  appoint to inquire into the issues involved in this dispute.\nThe board shall have powers and duties as set forth in Title I I  of \nsuch act. The board shall report to the President in accordance with \nthe provisions of Section 206 of such act on or before April 17,1967.\nUpon the su","path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/texts/cd-job-fr-originals-11344-ae10eaf4da.txt","sha256":"ecfdb4f91469969e4d4532d52f8600ffd47b291fc723ac7fb96d79f569b38158","source":{"line":2313,"path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"173cb39474abc272908bf377303be3c991dc0a77a0e4f9724b14559766fe10a6"}},{"first_1500_characters":"Instrument: EO:11344\nSource: https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1967-04-20/pdf/FR-1967-04-20.pdf\nSHA-256 of the downloaded file: ae10eaf4da356da4ac1c3df1512102f09efb2f9e508e6bcba9efe75739a91289\nLocation: 32 FR 6173, PDF pages 5-19 (confidence medium)\nMachine-extracted text layer of the official PDF (OCR for 1936-1994 scans). May contain recognition errors